  "strategy": "1. **Approach and Rationale**  \n   **Core Idea**: Balance local improvement and global exploration using delayed feedback from expensive function evaluations. This avoids early stagnation in the optimization landscape.  \n   - **Driver Selection**: Prioritize two-phase optimization (gradient-free exploration with `differential_evolution` followed by gradient-based refinement), augmented by random restarts and interpolation to survey diverse basins.  \n   - **Precision Control**: Integrate response surface modeling (RSM) to capture gradient steps incrementally, reducing peak computation while improving convergence.  \n   - **Transition**: Optimize a coarse grid for robust initial basins, then interpolate to fine grids for polishing, with hyperparameter schedules tailored to EDGD.  \n   - **Bottleneck Addressed**: Overcomes local optima by periodically reassessing function behavior via random restarts, ensuring gradient descent anchors to valid direction updates.\n\n2. **Mathematical Specification**  \n   - **Representation**: Piecewise step functions \\(h: [0, 2] \\to [0, 1]\\) represented by \\(n_{\\text{points}}\\) discrete samples.  \n   - **Objective**: Minimize \\(C_5 = \\max_k \\left( \\frac{2}{n} \\cdot \\operatorname{full\\_correlation}[k] \\right)\\), where \\(\\operatorname{full\\_correlation}[k]\\) is the discrete convolution of \\(h\\) with \\((1 - h)\\).  \n   - **Constraints**: \\(\\sum h[i] = n_{\\text{points}} / 2\\) and \\(0 \\leq h[i] \\leq 1\\) for all \\(i\\).  \n   - **Repair Function**: Projection via mean adjustment followed by bounded sort to ensure feasibility:  \n     \\(\\operatorname{repair}(x) = \\operatorname{clip}\\left(\\text{\\sc ProjectToSum}(\\mathrm{}, \\text{target}), 0, 1\\right)\\), with \\(\\text{ProjectToSum}\\) scaling the vector to achieve the desired sum.\n\n3. **Implementation Procedure**  \n   **Initialization**:  \n     - Start with a coarse grid \\(n_0 = 10\\) derived by downsampling the parent via \\(\\text{\\sc Downsample}\\) to 1/56th of the original length.  \n     - Phase 1 (Exploration): Use `differential_evolution` for 3\u00d7 parallel evaluations at \\(n_0 = 10\\) resolution.  \n     - **Repair**: Apply \\(\\operatorname{repair}\\) after each gradient descent update to maintain constraints.  \n\n   **Transitions**:  \n     - For each grid increase: Compute refined grid via \\(\\text{\\sc Upsample}(h, \\text{factor}) = h \\uparrow \\text{factor}\\).  \n     - Budget allocation: Coarser levels (\\( \\sim 0.3 \\times \\text{time} \\)) use stochastic search (`differential_evolution`); finer levels use gradient-based refinement (`Nelder-Mead` for \\(n=560\\)).\n\n4. **Search Choices and Variations**  \n   - **Randomized Restart**: Trigger by budget exhaustion or plateau detection (10% score stagnation) for 5 iterations.  \n   - **Response Surface Extrapolation**: Each restart estimates future evaluations via:  \n     \\( f_{\\text{next}} \\geq f_{\\text{best}}  \\text{with}  0.8 \\text{ confidence}\\), adjusting step sizes accordingly.\n\n5. **Compute Budget and Robustness**  \n   - Allocation:  \n     - Coarse\u63d0\u632f (4-level scheme): 20% budget.  \n     - Fine\u5206\u8fa8\u7387\u65f6\u95f4: Remaining 80% (200 s).  \n     - **Termination**: If optimization exceeds budget, fall back to the best-so-far solution.  \n   - **Fallback**: Use initial interpolation to restart.\n\n6. **Validation and Return Contract**  \n   **Post-Processing**:  \n     - Verify \\(\\text{\\sc Repair}\\) ensures \\(\\|h\\|_2 \\leq 1\\) and \\(\\sum h = n/2\\) with tolerance \\(10^{-6}\\).  \n     - Redetermine \\(C_5\\) using \\(\\text{\\sc FullCorrelation}\\) for top 100 lags.  \n   **Output**: Tuple (\\(h\\), final \\(C_5\\), \\(n_{\\text{points}}=560\\)).",
